{
 "summary": "Adds an upstream backport patch to `contrib/guix/patches` for `python-oscrypto` and applies it in `contrib/guix/manifest_codesign.scm`. This prevents a `ZeroDivisionError` during oscrypto's PBKDF2 timing test when building the code-signing environment from source without substitutes.",
 "problem": "Building `guix-codesign` without substitutes fails when building `oscrypto` 1.3.0 against OpenSSL 3.5.5. OpenSSL executes PBKDF2 benchmarks in less than a millisecond on fast machines, which oscrypto truncates to zero before using it as a divisor in `test_dump_private`.",
 "evidence": [
  "PR description and commit: 'With substitutes disabled, guix-codesign can fail when building oscrypto 1.3.0. The test_dump_private test raises ZeroDivisionError.'"
 ],
